# Odoo {{ odoo_version }} UI design: built-in first, usable on a phone

A screen's look is assembled from what the web client already ships, and every
view change is checked on a phone before it is called done.

Why:
- A stylesheet added for one form is ad hoc: that form stops looking like the
  rest, and the file still loads with `web.assets_backend` on every page.
- Rules aimed at the web client's own classes (`.o_inner_group`,
  `.o_list_table`, `.o_form_sheet`, `.o_kanban_record`) break when Odoo
  changes them; arch, widgets and utilities move with Odoo.
- Odoo's phone layout is built for its own elements only; custom styles are
  where it breaks.

Existing stylesheets in the repo predate this rule: no precedent for new work,
no cleanup target without a ticket. Website themes and QWeb PDF reports are
out of scope.

## The ladder

Take the first rung that delivers the intent:

1. **View arch** - `<group string="X">` (the title renders as Odoo's section
   separator), an outer `<group>` around inner ones for columns (two inner
   groups get `col-lg-6` each), `<notebook>`/`<page>`, `<separator>`,
   `<div class="oe_title"><h1>`, an image field with `class="oe_avatar"`,
   stat buttons in `<div name="button_box" class="oe_button_box">`,
   `<header>` with `widget="statusbar"`, chatter.
2. **Widgets** - the table below.
3. **Bootstrap utilities** on plain `<div>`s in the arch: grid (`row`,
   `col-*`, `g-*`), `card`, spacing, `border-*`, `text-*`, `bg-*`,
   `shadow-sm`, `d-flex`, `gap-*`, display (`d-none d-md-block`).
4. **Custom component** - only on the terms in "When custom code is fine".

## A mockup is intent, not code

A design from Claude Design, Figma or an HTML prototype says what the screen
must show. Map each element to the ladder; never port its CSS, hex colours,
fonts or pixel sizes. An element with no built-in counterpart is dropped or
raised with the user before any custom code is written.

| Mockup element | Built-in |
|---|---|
| Section with a heading | `<group string="X">`; coloured card: snippet below |
| Columns of fields | outer `<group>` + inner `<group>`s, or `row` / `col-*` |
| Status chip, pill | `widget="badge"` + `decoration-success/warning/danger/info/muted` |
| Coloured tags | `many2many_tags` + `options="{'color_field': 'color'}"` |
| Progress, score bar | `progressbar`, `percentpie`, `percentage` |
| Stage chevrons | `<header>` + `widget="statusbar"` |
| Switch | `boolean_toggle` |
| Stars | `priority` |
| 1..N rating buttons | selection + `widget="radio" options="{'horizontal': true}"` |
| Corner ribbon | `<widget name="web_ribbon" title="..." bg_color="bg-danger"/>` |
| KPI tiles on a record | stat buttons, `widget="statinfo"` |
| Info or warning banner | `<div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert">` |
| Avatar | image field `class="oe_avatar"`, `many2one_avatar_user` |
| Deadline colour | `remaining_days` |
| Card grid | kanban: `oe_kanban_global_click`, `o_kanban_record_top/_headings/_title/_body/_bottom`, `oe_kanban_bottom_left/_right` |
| Row colouring | `decoration-*` on `<{% if odoo_version in ['16.0', '17.0'] %}tree{% else %}list{% endif %}>`; `optional="show"`, `widget="handle"`, `sum="..."` |
| Charts | graph and pivot views in an action |

## Bootstrap in this Odoo

{% if odoo_version == '16.0' %}
- Bootstrap **5.1.3** (banner of `src/odoo/addons/web/static/lib/bootstrap/scss/bootstrap.scss`).
- Grid classes keep the stock breakpoints (`col-xxl-*` from 1400px). Odoo's
  own form CSS and the JS screen size (`ui` service) use a separate map,
  `$o-extra-grid-breakpoints` in `web/static/src/scss/primary_variables.scss`:
  `vsm` 475px added, `xxl` 1534px.
- No `fw-semibold` (5.2+): `fw-bold` or `fw-bolder`.
{% elif odoo_version == '19.0' %}
- Bootstrap **5.3.3** (banner in `src/odoo/addons/web/static/lib/bootstrap/scss/mixins/_banner.scss`).
- Stock breakpoints, `xxl` 1400px. `fw-semibold` exists.
{% else %}
- Read the version from the banner under `src/odoo/addons/web/static/lib/bootstrap/scss/`
  and the breakpoints from `web/static/src/scss/primary_variables.scss` before
  relying on a utility or a breakpoint.
{% endif %}
- Odoo adds utilities in `web/static/src/scss/utilities_custom.scss`, among
  them `rounded-top/-end/-bottom/-start`, `cursor-pointer`, `min-w-0`,
  `flex-basis-*`, `opacity-*-hover`; read the file for the rest.
- Border width and colour utilities apply to all four sides. One coloured
  side: `border-0 border-top border-3 border-info` - `border-0` clears every
  side, `border-top` restores one, the other three stay `none`.
- Breakpoints follow the viewport, not the sheet. Three `col-lg-4` cards at a
  1000px window measured 291px each and truncated many2one values;
  `col-12 col-xl-4` stacks them below 1200px.

## Coloured section cards without SCSS

Checked in the browser on 16.0 (computed style: top 3px solid, sides `none`):

```xml
<div class="row g-3 mb-4">
    <div class="col-12 col-xl-4">
        <div class="card h-100 border-0 border-top border-3 border-info shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body pb-1">
                <div class="text-uppercase small fw-bold border-bottom pb-2 mb-2">
                    <i class="fa fa-id-badge text-info me-2" title="Employee"/>Employee
                </div>
                <group name="employee_info">
                    <field name="job_id"/>
                </group>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <!-- next cards: border-warning + text-warning, border-success + text-success -->
</div>
```

Out of reach for utilities: a grey 1px frame beside a coloured top (the
colour applies to every side; `shadow-sm` stands in) and `letter-spacing`.
Accept the difference.

## On a phone

{% if odoo_version == '16.0' %}
Below 768px the web client switches to phone mode (`env.isSmall`,
`web/static/src/core/ui/ui_service.js`):
- An action opens its first kanban view instead of the list; without a kanban
  in its `view_mode` the phone gets the list table.
- The statusbar folds every stage into one dropdown. The button box shows 2
  stat buttons (4 up to 991px, 7 from 992px); the rest go under "More".
- Inner groups stack into one column below 992px.
{% endif %}
- An x2many with only an inline list stays a table on the phone. An inline
  kanban next to it gives cards on the phone and keeps the list on desktop:
  add one to any one2many people fill in on a phone.
- Hover-revealed controls have no touch path: a control a phone user needs is
  always visible.
- A fixed width (`style="width: ..."`, a wide `min-width`) pushes the page
  sideways at 375px.
- Secondary content is hidden on phones with display utilities
  (`d-none d-md-block`), not with a stylesheet.

## When custom code is fine

An OWL component with its own SCSS is acceptable when the request is very
specific and nothing like it is likely to be needed on another screen, and no
built-in renders it: an editable pricing matrix, a calculator grid.
Restyling a standard form, list or kanban never qualifies; those recur on
every screen. Say in the PR description why it qualifies.

Written like this:
- Inside the component, Bootstrap utilities carry what they can; the SCSS
  holds only the rest (a sticky column, fixed input widths).
- The file sits next to the component (`<name>.js`, `.xml`, `.scss`) and every
  rule nests under the component's root class. Odoo's own classes are touched
  only inside that root, never scoped by a class put on `<form>`.
- Colours come from variables (`$o-*`, Bootstrap theme variables,
  `var(--o-*)`), never hex literals; no `!important`.
- It passes the phone check like any view.

## Rejected in review

- Standard `<group>`s wrapped in custom card markup styled from a per-form
  class (`.o_x_form .o_x_section { ... }`): use the snippet above.
- A one2many or list restyled through `.o_list_table` (cell padding,
  `--bs-table-bg`, rounded row groups): decorations and widgets.
- Kanban cards repainted with hex colours: standard kanban classes, `badge`,
  `progressbar`.
- `style="..."` attributes or `!important` as a way around this skill.

## Verify before calling it done

- Phone: the browser pane's mobile preset (375x812, touch and a mobile user
  agent), page reloaded after switching. Passes when the page has no sideways
  scroll (`document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= innerWidth`), field values
  read without truncation, every action the user needs is reachable without
  hover, and each one2many is usable (cards or a narrow list).
- Desktop at about 1280px and 1600px. Column counts and truncation are
  measured, not assumed; where a utility combination matters, read
  `getComputedStyle`, not the class list.
- After `-u`, read the log for view-validator warnings: an `alert-*` without
  `role="alert|alertdialog|status"`, an `fa-*` icon with no `title`,
  `aria-label` or adjacent text, `btn` on a tag other than `a`, `button`,
  `select` or `input`.
- A hash-only URL change does not reload the web client, which keeps the old
  arch: change the query (`/web?r=1#...`).
{% if odoo_version == '16.0' %}
- A view written from `odoo shell` stays cached in the running server until
  `env.registry.clear_caches(); env.registry.signal_changes()` and a commit.
{% endif %}
